{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"fizzy-hypnotic-boto","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nNothing in rebar tracks eval spend in dollars. `usage_log.record()` (`src/rebar/llm/usage_log.py`) writes per-call token rows to `.rebar/usage.jsonl` only inside a gate session, `usage_report._price_row` can price rows via the optional `genai-prices` extra, the `rebar metrics` gate-economics lens counts calls not dollars, and there is no aggregate cap anywhere — the only limiter is the per-plan shed budget in `sizing.py`. This epic must stay under $200 on Bedrock, so the cap has to be enforced by the harness, not remembered by people.\n\n## Approach\n\nBuild `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/ledger.py`:\n\n- A committed ledger `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/ledger.jsonl`: one row per eval run (`run_id, tier, candidate, sample_n, started, finished, per-pass model ids, input/output/cache tokens, usd, price_table_version`) plus per-call rows in a git-ignored detail file. `cap_usd` and `reserve_usd` are constants in the module (200 / 30).\n- **Pre-flight**: each tier computes an estimate from stored corpus token counts × `genai-prices` current prices for the pinned Bedrock model ids; `ledger.reserve(estimate)` refuses (non-zero exit, clear message with remaining allocation) when `spent + estimate > cap − reserve`.\n- **Metering**: every eval run opens a usage-log session with `REBAR_USAGE_LOG` pointed at a per-run file; on completion the rows are priced and the ledger row finalised with actual spend; a run that dies mid-way is finalised from whatever rows exist on the next `ledger reconcile`.\n- `python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay ledger` prints spent / remaining / per-tier totals.\n\nAssume `genai-prices` Bedrock ids as the price source; the ledger records the price-table version so later re-pricing is possible.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/ledger.py` (new)\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/ledger.jsonl` (new)\n- `pyproject.toml` (the `pricing` extra becomes a dependency of the eval package's entry point)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_ledger.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: reserve succeeds under the cap and refuses over it with the remaining amount in the message; a finalised run's usd equals priced tokens; a crashed run is reconciled from partial rows; the cap and reserve are read from one place. No live calls needed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every Tier-1/Tier-2 run appears in the committed ledger with actual priced spend and per-pass model ids; checked by the ledger after the commissioning runs.\n- [ ] A run whose pre-flight estimate exceeds the remaining allocation is refused before any LLM call; checked by a unit test and by a manual dry-run with an artificially low cap.\n- [ ] `ledger` prints spent/remaining and the total never exceeds $200 across the epic; checked at epic close.\n- [ ] Unit tests pass in `make test`.","id":"4c80-edd3-20f1-4dff","parent_id":"759e-7dc1-675c-4877","priority":1,"tags":["plan-review","evals","budget","bedrock"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Eval budget ledger: price every eval call, pre-flight estimates, refuse runs that would exceed the $200 cap"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788029178453660801,"uuid":"ca501f76-e5b5-4cb7-a21b-e1b3779a34b2"}